  "limits": [
    "MCP reads existing sanitized network metadata only. Capture must be started in Network and network sharing separately approved. No capture-control, replay, settings or traffic-write tool exists.",
    "Results contain the newest matching entries, oldest first within the result; capped at 100 entries or 128 KiB, with matched/truncated and capture retention metadata. No pagination cursor or automatic capture.",
    "Native suites cover HTTP metadata, separate consent, both transports, filters, revocation, stopped/live capture and immutable stopped-session data. Unit tests cover byte bounds, storage failures and pending-read revocation.",
    "Tests use installed browsers, owned localhost fixtures, temporary profiles and deny proxies. No public threat sites or personal browser profiles were used. This does not configure or approve the user's actual MCP client/browser connection.",
    "The first focused unit run failed on one old six-tool assertion, which was updated for the seventh read-only tool. The first passing Chrome run preceded the cached-size optimization, final documentation and the final runtime-error assertion; its snapshot is retained separately."
